content.content:
  -only string
    	glob on the fixture names, without .http, e.g. catalog-* (default every fixture)
  -request-timeout duration
    	how long one request may take, connection included; ask for 45s when the upstream is cut, its first read takes 20 s (default 15s)
  -rest-host string
    	loopback address the bench is reached on (default 127.0.0.1); record accepts a loopback address only, because the bench credentials always go through 127.0.0.1
  -secrets string
    	secrets file, outside the repository (default under $XDG_STATE_HOME/devdesk/nexus-bench)
  -state value
    	state the bench is in, nominal or upstream-cut: reads the upstream from the cluster (read only), refuses a bench in another state, and records only the fixtures of that state (default no state: nothing is read and no fixture is filtered)
Usage: nexus-bench down [flags]

Delete the bench namespace, wait until it is gone, then remove its stored passwords.

A flag beats its NEXUS_BENCH_* variable, which beats the default.
